From 8813c39e2482be82f8786151a56df4dce8e0a523 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Al Sayed Hoota <78100282+AlsayedHoota@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Apr 2026 11:06:12 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(session_search): load content from FTS-matched
 session, not empty compaction root

Context compaction creates chains of sessions linked via parent_session_id.
The previous code resolved FTS matches to the root of the chain for both
deduplication AND content loading. This was broken because:

1. Search: The root session is often empty (0 messages) after compaction.
   Loading conversation from the root yielded nothing, silently dropping
   valid search results. Now we use the lineage root only for dedup and
   load content from the session where FTS actually found the match.

2. Recent listing: All sessions with parent_session_id were hidden, which
   excluded the leaf sessions of compaction chains (where the real
   conversation lives). Now we only skip intermediate compression nodes
   (end_reason='compression') and show the leaf.

Added _get_lineage_ids() helper to walk parent chains. Added two new tests
for compaction chain search and deduplication.

Fixes: sessions with context compaction (sometimes 5-10 levels deep)
were invisible to both session_search queries and recent session listings.
