From dac7edeecf43fe910ed34d798cd2a479e9b06949 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Al Sayed Hoota <78100282+AlsayedHoota@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Apr 2026 11:24:21 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] address review: fix lineage walk, include_children, root
 filtering, dedup, tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Address all 6 Copilot review comments on PR #5447:

1. _get_lineage_ids now walks BOTH directions (up to root, then BFS down
   to all descendants) so current-session exclusion works regardless of
   whether the active session is a root or leaf.

2. CRITICAL: Pass include_children=True to list_sessions_rich() — without
   this, sessions with parent_session_id were filtered out by SQL before
   our Python logic ever saw them, making the recent-listing fix a no-op.

3. Skip ANY session with end_reason='compression', not just those with
   parent_session_id. Root fragments can also be empty compression nodes.

4. Replace unreliable min(lineage) chain key with explicit
   _resolve_to_lineage_root() walk. Extracted the inline _resolve_to_root
   closure into a module-level _resolve_to_lineage_root() to eliminate
   duplication and ensure consistent behavior.

5. Fixed misleading test docstring on
   test_current_root_session_excludes_child_lineage.

6. Added TestRecentSessionsCompaction class with 4 tests:
   - test_leaf_shown_intermediates_hidden
   - test_dedup_same_chain
   - test_current_session_lineage_excluded
   - test_normal_sessions_unaffected

All 31 tests pass.
